<Base title="The Data That Matters"><section class="interior"><div class="eyebrow">WORK / WORKSHOP FRAMEWORK</div><h1>The Data That Matters</h1><p class="lede">Start with business strategy. Measure what matters.</p><p class="lede" style="font-size:16px">A working session for leaders who need a shared definition of success before building another dashboard.</p><div class="callout"><h2>Where we start</h2><p>Developed through dozens of working sessions across multiple organizations, this is an adaptable approach, not a fixed presentation or a prepackaged dashboard.</p><p>We begin with the decisions the business needs to make. Then we work backward to the information, definitions, owners, and systems that support those decisions.</p></div><div class="callout"><h2>If you could only track three things, what would they be?</h2><p>Not the three easiest numbers to pull. The three measures that would tell you whether your strategy is working (and help you decide what to do next).</p><p>That choice starts the conversation. We bring leaders together to agree on what success looks like, test whether they mean the same thing by the same numbers, and trace the data back to its sources.</p></div><div class="callout"><h2>What the work produces</h2><p>Shared business priorities, a common measurement vocabulary, visibility into conflicting definitions or missing inputs, clearer ownership, and a practical sequence for improving reporting and decision-making.</p><p>The point isn't more data. It's a better conversation about the business, supported by information people can use.</p></div><p><a href="/work/">← Back to Work</a></p></section></Base>
